pothalamus glucopenia triggers counterregulatory hormone release. <source>Diabetes</source> 1995 <volume>44</volume>: <fpage>180</fpage>&#x02013;184, <year>1995</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7859938</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Borg MA, Sherwin RS, Borg WP, Tamborlane WV, Shulman GI: Local ventromedial hypothalamus glucose perfusion blocks counterregulation during systemic hypoglycemia in awake rats. <source>J Clin Invest</source> <volume>99</volume>: <fpage>361</fpage>&#x02013;536, <year>1997</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9006005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Smith D, Amiel SA: The anatomy of the human hypoglycaemia sensor. <source>Diabetes Nutr Metab</source> <volume>15</volume>: <fpage>316</fpage>&#x02013;318, <year>2002</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12625477</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">McCrimmon R: The mechanisms that underlie glucose sensing during hypoglycaemia in diabetes. <source>Diabet Med</source> <volume>25</volume>: <fpage>513</fpage>&#x02013;522, <year>2008</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18312421</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Donovan CM, Hamilton-Wessler M, Halter JB, Bergman RN: Primacy of liver glucosensors in the sympathetic response to progressive hypoglycemia. <source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source> <volume>91</volume>: <fpage>2863</fpage>&#x02013;2867, <year>1994</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8146201</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hevener AL, Bergman RN, Donovan CM: Novel glucosensor for hypoglycemic detection localized to the portal vein. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>46</volume>: <fpage>1521</fpage>&#x02013;1525, <year>1997</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9287058</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hevener AL, Bergman RN, Donovan CM: Hypoglycemic detection does not occur in the hepatic artery or liver: findings consistent with a portal vein glucosensor locus. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>50</volume>: <fpage>399</fpage>&#x02013;403, <year>2001</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11272153</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal">Saberi M, Bohland M, Donovan CM: The locus for hypoglycemic detection shifts with the rate of fall in glycemia: the role of portal-superior mesenteric vein glucose sensing. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>57</volume>: <fpage>1380</fpage>&#x02013;1386, <year>2008</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18292347</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal">Fanelli CG, Pampanelli S, Porcellati F, Bartocci L, Scionti L, Rossetti P, Bolli GB: Rate of fall of blood glucose and physiological responses of counterregulatory hormones, clinical symptoms and cognitive function to hypoglycaemia in type I diabetes mellitus in the postprandial state. <source>Diabetologia</source> <volume>46</volume>: <fpage>53</fpage>&#x02013;64, <year>2003</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12637983</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal">Matveyenko AV, Donovan CM: Metabolic sensors mediate hypoglycemic detection at the portal vein. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>55</volume>: <fpage>1276</fpage>&#x02013;1282, <year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16644683</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal">McGuire E, Helderman J, Tobin J, Andres R, Berman M: Effects of arterial venous sampling on analysis of glucose kinetics in man. <source>J Appl Physiol</source> <volume>41</volume>: <fpage>565</fpage>&#x02013;573, <year>1976</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">985402</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r30"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal">Mitrako